  "body": "<p>Kratom tea can appear on a kava bar menu because the lounge serves more than one kind of botanical beverage. At Tribal Kava Lounge in West Palm Beach, kava and kratom have separate menu categories, alongside fruit drinks without either botanical. The name of the venue tells you where you are meeting; the description of the individual drink tells you what you are ordering.</p>\n<p>That distinction matters when you are new to the menu. A friend might say, \u201cWe are going for kava,\u201d while the people at the table choose several different drinks. Ask about your own cup rather than assuming everybody is ordering the same ingredient. Tribal&#x27;s kratom products are for adults 21+ only, with valid ID required.</p>\n<h2>Kava and kratom are different ingredients</h2>\n<p>Kava is made from the root of the kava plant. Kratom beverages are made from the leaves of Mitragyna speciosa. They are separate botanical ingredients, even when both appear behind the same counter. A crafted drink can also look different from a straightforward tea without becoming a different plant.</p>\n<p>Use our <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/kava-vs-kratom\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">kava-versus-kratom guide</a> for the basic distinction, then ask the team which base is in the menu item you are considering. If somebody says \u201cbotanical tea,\u201d it is reasonable to ask which botanical they mean. A clear answer is more helpful than trying to decode the name from the color of the drink.</p>\n<h2>What does brewed kratom tea mean on Tribal&#x27;s menu?</h2>\n<p>Tribal lists brewed kratom tea separately from crafted kratom drinks. The tea section offers red, white, and green leaf choices, with small and large serving formats. Start by asking the team to explain the available tea options and what the menu labels refer to.</p>\n<p>Those labels are not a shortcut to promising a particular personal experience. They identify options on the menu; they do not tell the whole story about an individual drink. Ask about ingredients, preparation, and the available format instead of relying on something you heard secondhand about a color name.</p>\n<h2>A crafted kratom drink is another presentation</h2>\n<p>The crafted kratom section includes named drinks such as Mango Chili Lime, Passionfruit Mint, and Blackberry Dragonfruit Fizz. The menu describes their flavor combinations. A crafted format gives you a different way to choose a drink while keeping its kratom base clear.</p>\n<p>Read the complete description before choosing. A fruit-forward name does not mean a drink has no botanicals. Likewise, the separate fruit-drink section is useful when you want a drink with no kava and no kratom. The <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/menu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">current menu</a> helps you compare the categories without collapsing them into one long list of colorful names.</p>\n<h2>Ask about the item, not just the category</h2>\n<p>Three questions make a menu conversation easier: \u201cWhat is the base?\u201d \u201cWhat else is in this drink?\u201d and \u201cWhich size or format does this item come in?\u201d If you need an ingredient excluded or have a food allergy, ask the team to confirm the specific recipe before ordering.</p>\n<p>Do not assume that brewed tea, a crafted drink, and another listed kratom format are interchangeable. A similar price or a smaller cup does not make two items the same. Let the team explain the exact item you are looking at. You are choosing a drink, not completing a speed round where asking a follow-up costs points.</p>\n<h2>The lounge experience can be bigger than one beverage</h2>\n<p>The social part of a kava lounge is the shared place: a table, a conversation, or an activity you came to join. People can spend time together while choosing different menu categories. That is part of what makes a clear menu useful for groups; everybody can ask questions and make their own choice.</p>\n<p>For a first visit, read the <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/new-here\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">new-guest guide</a>. For an activity, check the current <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/events\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">event announcements</a>. Tribal is at 770 S Military Trail, Unit A1, West Palm Beach. Arrive with the questions that matter to you, and use the counter conversation to understand your order before settling into the room.</p>\n<h2>Sources and local details</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/menu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tribal menu</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/what-is-kratom\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tribal kratom explainer</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/new-here\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">First-visit guide</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://www.thetribalkavalounge.com/events\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tribal events</a></p>\n<p><strong>Responsible use:</strong> Kratom products are for adults 21+ only. Valid ID required. Products are not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. Do not mix kava or kratom with alcohol or other substances. If you are pregnant, nursing, taking medications, or have health concerns, speak with a qualified professional.</p>",
